From adcda32e9823c66fb86ec3fae65120e1c98c76b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bogdan Lapadat <lapadat.bogdanv@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:06:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] qwen35 hybrid: opt-in CPU/GPU split of the CPU-side
 experts (STRATA_Q36_SPLIT), decode timers (STRATA_Q36_DTIME)

STRATA_Q36_SPLIT=1: per one-token decode layer, a share of the experts the CPU pool would compute
is copied from the pinned RAM tier to a VRAM stage on a separate stream and computed with the slot
experts kernel while the pool computes the rest. STRATA_Q36_SPLIT_FRAC fixes the share; unset, it
is balanced per token so the pool time matches the copy time. The RAM tier is page-aligned and
registered with the GPU when the split is on. STRATA_Q36_SPLIT_CHECK=1 also computes the streamed
rows (and one slot row as a reference) on the pool and reports the relative L2 difference.

STRATA_Q36_DTIME=1: per decode token host timers (router wait, pool, greedy sync), CPU expert
bytes, pool bandwidth and page faults, printed at the end of a serve request.

Also STRATA_Q36_PROFILE_DECODE_ONLY: the routing profile counts generated tokens only.
